 "_doc": "Phobetor (Ovid 11.638-641): \"called Icelus by the gods, Phobetor by mortal men\", who becomes a beast, a bird or a long serpent: the bringer of nightmares. As a beast, a shaggy black wolf-thing with a bristling mane, a cluster of glowing eyes, gaping fanged jaws and smoke trailing from it; as a bird, a huge ragged black bird with a hooked beak, its wings spread wide; as a serpent, a long striped serpent rearing from its coils, crested and fanged. Built by tools/art/build_heavens.py.",
